      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There remains a lively and legitimate scientific debate, particularly concerning the biological bases of gender identity, with researchers studying neurodiversity, fetal development, and endocrinology to better understand how biology and psychology interact. While many experts reject non-scientific political arguments, there is no uniform global consensus; instead, there is a vast array of ongoing research regarding whether our secondary sex characteristics and brain structures fully align with these identities. Therefore, individuals who question the extent of the \"spectrum\" are often engaging in active scientific inquiry rather than being flatly labeled as anti-science, as the field continues to evolve new data and theories.",
      "source": "target",
